- IC1 `replace ^= with |= in xor_in_place` — `mkdir -p target/inverse-control && f=crates/conductor-emit/src/identity.rs && cp "$f" target/inverse-control/identity.rs.bak && trap 'cp target/inverse-control/identity.rs.bak crates/conductor-emit/src/identity.rs' EXIT && sed -i 's/\*byte ^= m;/*byte |= m;/' "$f" && test "$(grep -cF '*byte |= m;' "$f")" = 1 && { cargo nextest run -p conductor-emit --lib --profile ci -E 'test(=identity::tests::rekey_under_one_salt_twice_restores_every_id)'; test $? -eq 100; }` — killed when it exits 0 with a `FAIL [` line naming `identity::tests::rekey_under_one_salt_twice_restores_every_id` (nextest exit 100 = tests failed; 101 would be a build failure, which proves nothing). - IC2 `replace ^= with &= in xor_in_place` — IC1 with the replacement `*byte \&= m;` (the `&` escaped: an unescaped `&` re-inserts the match) and the count check on `*byte &= m;`; same test, same reading. - IC3 `replace > with >= in emit_canary_storms` — IC1's shape on `crates/conductor-run/src/canary.rs` (backup `canary.rs.bak`), `sed -i 's/if n > 0 {/if n >= 0 {/'`, count check on `if n >= 0 {`, filter `test(=canary::tests::the_first_storm_leaves_at_the_call_with_no_gap_before_it)` under `cargo nextest run -p conductor-run --lib --profile ci`. - IC4 `replace * with + in emit_canary_storms` — IC3's shape with `sed -i 's/n \* CANARY_STORM_COUNT/n + CANARY_STORM_COUNT/'`, count check on `n + CANARY_STORM_COUNT`, filter `test(=canary::tests::every_real_model_canary_occurrence_carries_its_own_span_identity)`. - IC5 `replace * with / in emit_canary_storms` — IC4 with `sed -i 's/n \* CANARY_STORM_COUNT/n / CANARY_STORM_COUNT/'` and the count check on `n / CANARY_STORM_COUNT`. - CARRY-sh — `mkdir -p target/carry && f=crates/conductor-emit/src/identity.rs && cp "$f" target/carry/identity.rs.bak && trap 'cp target/carry/identity.rs.bak crates/conductor-emit/src/identity.rs' EXIT && printf '
#[allow(dead_code)]
fn planted_lint(v: &[u8]) -> bool {
    v.len() == 0
}
' >> "$f" && { bash scripts/agent-run.sh run; test $? -eq 101; }`. It is measured when it exits 0 with clippy's `len_zero` error line (`length comparison to zero`) printed at the workspace clippy line. Record the bare exit (101) and that printed line verbatim, host paths elided.
